#undef NDEBUG
// Review GX: pm4py's eventually-follows graph of an upload with another
// timestamp key, an explicit start key, or XES ints past int64.
//
// - eventually_follows_timestamp_attribute=K is
//   discover_eventually_follows_graph(frame, timestamp_key=K): the frame's
//   check of K (a column, datetime64, no gap) first, then the pairs of a
//   case kept where K of the earlier row is at most the later row's start
//   (the frame's start_timestamp column, else K); Polars' copy sorts by case
//   and K with its unstable sort and keeps every pair (its default too), and
//   raises a DuplicateError for K = start_timestamp.
// - eventually_follows_start_attribute=S is the log variant on
//   convert_to_event_log of the frame (the Polars copy on the lazy shape) as
//   Python runs it: each trace sorted by S, then each event's completion
//   compared by `<=` with each later start; KeyError and TypeError as Python
//   raises them.
// - XES ints past INT64_MAX typed as pandas types them (uint64, float64 or
//   object).
//
// Expected values are pm4py 2.7.22 black-box on the same inputs
// (review-harness round-gx: tc/mkgx.py, ct/efg2.py).
//
// Usage: minera_server_review_gx_tests <minera_server>

